CONDITIONAL CLEARANCE INSIGHT:
  P(lonely) = Π P_k where P_k = conditional clearance of runner k.
  Each P_k ≈ (n-2)/n ≈ 86% (for n=7).
  The product ≈ ((n-2)/n)^{n-1} = outside credit ≈ 13%.

  For INITIAL SEGMENT: P_k is EXACTLY (n-2)/n for each k
  (the runners are perfectly equidistributed within the feasible set).
  Product = outside credit exactly. But the lonely measure is 0
  (wall-only) — the product measures the EXPECTED fraction, not
  the actual fraction.

  For NON-AP speed sets: the P_k values DEVIATE from (n-2)/n.
  Some are higher, some lower. The product can be larger or smaller
  than the outside credit. LRC says: the product (or wall hits)
  is always positive.

