THE PRODUCT FORMULA:
  P(lonely) = Π_k P_k where P_k = cond prob of runner k safe.

  Each P_k ≈ (n-2)/n with small correction ε_k.
  The corrections encode the INTER-RUNNER DEPENDENCE.

  For the INITIAL SEGMENT: corrections are EXACTLY zero!
  (Each runner is equidistributed within the feasible set.)
  Product = outside credit = ((n-2)/n)^{n-1} > 0. ✓

  For NON-AP speed sets: corrections are nonzero but small.
  The p-adic tree bounds them: ε_k ≤ C × p^{-level(k)}.
  The sum Σ ε_k converges → product > 0 → lonely. ✓

  THIS IS THE GLOBAL→LOCAL BRIDGE:
  Global spread = each P_k > 0 (each runner likely safe)
  Local emptiness = product > 0 (ALL runners safe simultaneously)
  The tree ensures the product doesn't collapse to 0
  because the factors are nearly independent (p-adic decay).

